# PSGrouper line-ending and diff policy
#
# Verified before adding: all 32 tracked blobs are already LF-only in storage, so the
# rules below change nothing that is committed. They make the existing behaviour explicit
# instead of leaving it to each clone's local core.autocrlf setting -- a clone with
# autocrlf=false, or on a non-Windows host, would otherwise check out LF and drift from
# the rest of the tree, which is uniformly CRLF.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Text: stored LF in the repository, checked out CRLF in the working tree.
# Covers .ps1, .psm1, .psd1, .ps1xml, .md, LICENSE.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Code signing does not interact with these rules. The source is deliberately unsigned;
# Build.ps1 signs the copies it stages into release/ (the manifest, the format file and a
# generated .cat catalog), and release/ is gitignored. So git never handles a signed file,
# and no path needs to be exempted from the text rule above to keep a signature intact.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary: never normalize, never diff as text. ("binary" == "-text -diff".)
#
# Nothing binary is tracked -- .gitignore excludes lib/ (the bundled .NET runtime and
# GrouperLib assemblies) and release/. These rules are insurance for a future
# `git add -f`, so a stray assembly or signed catalog cannot be corrupted by line-ending
# conversion on the way in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pdb binary
*.cat binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Diff hunk headers. Git has no built-in driver for PowerShell, so .ps1/.psm1 use the
# default; only markdown gets one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.md text diff=markdown
